@@ -28,4 +28,15 @@ moving a value into its own child (moving a value onto itself is a no-op), or a
 error nothing is returned. Pointers follow the rules above, so only own members are ever touched and
 `__proto__` is an ordinary member name.
 
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Merge Patch to a parsed
+JSON document and returns the merged document as a new value; neither argument is mutated. Object
+patches merge member by member, a `null` member deletes that member, and any other patch value
+(including an array) replaces the target. A non-object target is treated as `{}` when the patch is an
+object, so `null`s inside it are dropped. Only own members are considered and `__proto__` is an
+ordinary member name. Note that a merge patch cannot set a member to `null`.
+
+It throws a `TypeError` when the patch is not JSON (such as `undefined` or `NaN`).
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
